    "finding": "the plaintext DLG solution, mapped through Nr, matches the MASKED gradients with an identical gradient-match loss and recovers the identical token via NN over E_tilde. Gradient inversion is therefore exactly as (in)effective in the masked basis as in plaintext \u2014 the orthogonal mask is a transparent change of basis. Privacy against gradient inversion comes from batch aggregation + not exposing per-example gradients, NOT from the mask.",
